=== OBSERVATIONS (beyond scope; NOT grounds for FAIL) ===
1. The test's "visible text node" guard at line 64 includes
   `strings.Contains(body, 'data-spending-apply="current" class=')`, which is
   attribute-ORDER dependent and would break on a cosmetic attribute reorder
   that changes no behavior. The load-bearing assertion (label extracted from
   the button's inner text, line 52) is order-independent and is what
   mutation-killed, so the guard's brittleness is cosmetic only.
2. Not verifiable by any command I can run here: that "Keep current plan" is
   the wording the user wants. It matches the brief's spec string byte for byte.
3. The rendered body contains 4 aria-label attributes elsewhere in the results
   partial; none of them is on any of the 5 data-spending-apply buttons
   (proven by the five full <form> dumps above), so WCAG 2.5.3 Label in Name
   is satisfied for the changed control. Full a11y adjudication belongs to
   checker-a11y, the other named checker.
